analysis/rivers.jl (25 Nov) found every JRA55 river delivered, but its water lands 80-100 km from its mouth on
average and only 30-60 % within 30 km of the coast, while the runs are too salty in strips along the river-fed coasts
with fresher water offshore. Two twins of config_sep2005_4mo_nemo_glorys12_nz100.toml with [land]
river_spread_degrees = 0.5 and 0.3 (patch 097), same NumericalEarth as that run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AbhhvmHjZYCHhFxumZ9A47
